+- [PostgreSQL: `ALTER TABLE`](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/17/sql-altertable.html) — `ADD CONSTRAINT
+  … NOT VALID` and `VALIDATE CONSTRAINT`, and the lock level each takes: the whole reason the
+  contract can be applied to a table that is being written to.
+- [PostgreSQL: explicit locking](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/17/explicit-locking.html) — the lock
+  levels a migration's statements take, and which of them queue behind a running query.
+- `relay/2.23-online-schema` — the same three phases when the middle one is a command somebody runs
+  rather than a queue's own work.
+- `jobq/3.11-delayed-timers` — `run_at`, the column the rate above is written with.
+
+## What this page is compared with
+
+`jobq/3.23-online-schema` has a spec that reads this file and compares it with the project's own
+constants: the three metric names (`jobq::engine::PLAN_METRICS`), the two bounds
+(`BURST_LIMIT` and `RESUME_LIMIT`), and the three phases by name. A budget whose names live in a
+page, a harness and a baseline is a budget that drifts, so the three are read against one list.
